    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "So Washington makes a calculation. If it can't control the oil, it can try to control the money the oil produces. In July nineteen seventy four, the new Treasury Secretary, William Simon, flies to Saudi Arabia, the most powerful oil producer in the region. What comes out of those meetings shapes the next fifty years. Saudi Arabia keeps selling its oil in dollars, and backs dollar pricing across OPEC. It takes the flood of dollars it earns and invests a huge share of them back into America, buying U.S. government debt. In return, America offers weapons, investment, and security cooperation with the kingdom.",
